# BALANCE REMEDIATION PLAYBOOK
### Beyond Depth Reconstruction — 1.21.1 / NeoForge 21.1.249
**Written 2026-08-28. Companion to the audit doc. This is the "what to actually change" file.**

---

## ⚠ READ THIS BEFORE YOU TRUST A SINGLE NUMBER BELOW

The tuning-data payload handed to this doc was **empty**:

```json
{"tuning":[],"remedies":[],"spine":[],"offenders":[]}
```

No per-mod config keys, no researched remediation plans, no offender list, no modlist. So
everything in Section 2 that isn't traceable to the recon briefs is **derived, inferred, or
templated** — not measured. Every config path is marked with a confidence level. Nothing here
should be pasted into a live server without the verification step attached to it.

What IS hard-verified and load-bearing:
- L_Ender's Cataclysm gear/boss stats (from the official wiki, via the North Star brief).
- Vanilla netherite/Sharpness arithmetic (trivially checkable in-game).
- Ars 'n Spells config keys and defaults (from its own README).
- 1.21.1 datapack format facts (pack_format 48, singular directory names, data-driven enchantments).

What is **NOT** verified and is flagged inline as `⚠ VERIFY BEFORE APPLYING`:
- Every mod config file path and TOML key name.
- Every hours estimate in the parity table.
- The existence and stats of "Antarchy" content (the owner named it; I have zero primary data on it).

**The single highest-value action in this entire document is not a config edit — it is
Section 6.1: measure the real numbers before changing anything.** A playbook built on
guessed numbers produces a pack balanced against a fiction.

---

# 1. THE PARITY PHILOSOPHY

## 1.0 What this pack is

**This pack is a HUB, not a SPINE.** Six players walk up to a menu of simultaneous tracks and
pick one. Nobody finishes everything. Nobody is required to do track A before track B.

That premise makes exactly one thing sacred, and it is not power level. It is **rate**.

> The failure mode: *"2 people do one mod and 2 people do another and put in equal effort but
> get completely different rewards."*

A 40-damage sword after 80 hours is fine. A 40-damage sword after 10 hours is broken. **Absolute
ceiling is nearly irrelevant. Payoff-per-hour is everything.**

And the corollary that gets forgotten: **under-rewarding is a defect of equal severity.** If Dan
sinks 60 hours into Create and comes out weaker than DJ did in 20 hours of Deeper and Darker,
Dan was robbed and the pack failed — even though nothing was "overpowered." Fixes go in both
directions.

---

## 1.1 The metric

### Definitions

**P — Power multiplier over netherite.**
Baseline `P = 1.00` is defined as **a Sharpness V netherite sword in full enchanted netherite
armor**, i.e. the endgame a player reaches with zero content mods. Arithmetic:

```
Netherite sword base       :  8.0 damage × 1.6 attack speed = 12.8 sustained DPS
+ Sharpness V (+3.25 flat) : 11.25 damage × 1.6 attack speed = 18.0 sustained DPS   ← P = 1.00
```

P for a track's reward is that reward's **effective combat-equivalent throughput** divided by
18.0 DPS, including its ability/utility rider, not just its stat line.

Worked example, the anchor:

```
Cataclysm Void Forge       : 13.0 damage × 1.0 attack speed = 13.0 DPS
+ Sharpness V              : 16.25 damage × 1.0             = 16.25 DPS  → 0.90 raw
+ AoE hammer slam (13 dmg, 4-block radius, shield-break, 4s CD)
+ Void Runes (35 runes, 7 magic dmg, hits twice)
+ unbreakable, netherite-tier pickaxe
                                                        → effective P ≈ 1.35
```

**Note what that means:** Cataclysm's endgame boss-drop weapon is a **sidegrade** on raw DPS and
only reaches 1.35x once you count the utility. That is a mod author choosing restraint on
purpose, and it is why Cataclysm is the yardstick and not a defendant.

**H — Hours invested.** Wall-clock hours for one player of average skill to go from "decided to
do this track" to "holding the track's characteristic reward."

**T — Tedium coefficient.** Effort ≠ hours. 60 hours of tense boss fights is not the same
investment as 60 hours of grinding andesite.

| T | Character | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **0.8** | Tense, skill-expressive, memorable | Boss gauntlets, arena fights |
| **0.9** | Exploration with real stakes | Dungeon delving, dimension traversal |
| **1.0** | Mixed / neutral | Most content |
| **1.2** | Repetitive with variance | RNG affix farming, loot rerolling |
| **1.3** | Flat grind | Resource automation as a prerequisite, ore-count gates |

`H_eff = H × T`. Higher tedium raises effective cost, which **lowers** R, which correctly flags
a grindy track as under-rewarding and demands a buff or a shortening.

**R — Parity Rate.**

```
R = (P − 1.0) / H_eff
```

Units: netherite-multiples of *gain* per effort-hour. This is the number that goes in the table
and the number that gets checked when someone proposes mod #151.

---

## 1.2 Deriving the target band — the arithmetic

Anchor on Cataclysm, because it is the one track in this pack whose numbers are wiki-verified
and whose author demonstrably tuned for restraint.

```
Cataclysm full boss gauntlet → Void Forge
  P      = 1.35
  ΔP     = 0.35
  H      = 40 hours   (8 bosses, dungeon-gated, group play)
  T      = 0.8        (boss fights: high tension, low tedium)
  H_eff  = 40 × 0.8 = 32
  R*     = 0.35 / 32 = 0.01094
```

**Anchor rate R\* = 0.011.**

> ### 🔴 STOP — the anchor's `P = 1.35` is a GUESS, and the whole band inherits it
>
> *(Added by completeness review. This box is the most important correction in the document.)*
>
> `P = 1.35` decomposes into **`0.90` (wiki-sourced arithmetic — solid)** plus **`+0.45` for
> "AoE + shield-break + unbreakable + pickaxe" — a number with no derivation anywhere in this
> project.** It was chosen, not computed.
>
> This document flags `H = 40` as an estimate. **It does not flag `P = 1.35`, and it should.**
> That asymmetry is what makes `R* = 0.011` look measured when it is one judgment call wearing
> three significant figures.
>
> **Sensitivity — how much the verdicts move if the utility allowance is wrong:**
>
> | Utility allowance | P | R\* | Green band | What flips |
> |---|---|---|---|---|
> | +0.20 (conservative) | 1.10 | **0.0031** | 0.0013 – 0.0050 | 🔴 **Half the ✅ rows in §1.3 become "over band."** Undergarden, YUNG's, Artifacts all break upward. |
> | **+0.45 (this doc)** | **1.35** | **0.0109** | **0.005 – 0.018** | *as written* |
> | +0.70 (generous) | 1.60 | **0.0188** | 0.0075 – 0.0300 | 🔵 Apotheosis (0.0417) drops from 3.8× to 2.2× over; **Create's under-floor verdict gets worse.** |
>
> **A third of the ✅/🔴 verdicts in §1.3 are decided by a number nobody computed.**
>
> **How to use this document anyway** (the band is still useful, just not precise):
> 1. **Act only on tracks that miss the band by >2×.** Those survive every column above:
>    Iron's Spells, Apotheosis, Simply Swords, Create. That is your real fix list.
> 2. **Ignore the yellow and band-edge rows entirely** until the anchor is measured. Tuning
>    Undergarden vs Deeper and Darker (§2.7, a 1.5× gap) against a ±3× uncertain band is noise.
> 3. **Re-derive after measurement.** §5 fix #2 measures `H`. Also measure `P` — kill the same
>    200 HP dummy with a Sharp V netherite sword and with a Void Forge *using its ability on
>    cooldown*, and use the real time ratio. That converts the guess to data in one session.
>
> **Second, smaller correction:** the ±60% band width is also arbitrary — justified only as
> "roughly the point at which a power difference stops reading as 'different build'." That is a
> reasonable intuition and it is not evidence. Treat the band as a **soft advisory**, not a gate.
>
> **Third:** this document's `P = 1.35` for the Void Forge **contradicts `00-MODLIST-AUDIT.md`,
> which uses `P = 0.90` and concludes Cataclysm needs a BUFF while this document concludes it is
> the healthy ANCHOR that needs no change.** Both cannot be acted on. See Doc 00 §0.5 for the
> full reconciliation. **Short version: report both numbers — `0.90` raw, `~1.35` with utility —
> and never quote one without the other.**

Band width: ±60% of anchor. 60% is chosen because it is roughly the point at which a power
difference stops reading as "different build" and starts reading as "you got cheated" —
a 1.6x rate gap over a 30-hour track is a full netherite-tier of separation.

```
Lower bound = 0.011 × 0.40 = 0.0044  →  round to 0.005
Upper bound = 0.011 × 1.60 = 0.0176  →  round to 0.018
```

### ✅ GREEN BAND: `0.005 ≤ R ≤ 0.018`
### 🟡 YELLOW: `0.002–0.005` or `0.018–0.030` — fix on the next maintenance pass
### 🔴 RED: `R < 0.002` or `R > 0.030` — fix before launch

